{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -A 35 -B 2 'D417|D436' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"4604-- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step. It amends the shape D409 gave an event's answer, if it passes.\n4605-\n4606:## D417 · 2026-11-10 · A figure for a rolling twelve months with no publication day in the texts is declined\n4607-\n4608-- **Asked:** \"有两道题问的是“某项调查统计的未来 12 个月里，中国企业把多少 AI 芯片预算给国产”。这不是整年数字，文章也没说后续调查哪天公布。到期日改由程序定之后，系统对这两道题基本不出题了（6 次里 5 次），理由是“没有能核对的公布日期”。这是新出现的行为，你还没确认过；两位裁决读者对它也意见相反，第 4 条线过不过就取决于它。怎么定？\"\n4609-  - Options: confirm, no judged question (recommended): \"滚动 12 个月、又没有公布日期的数字，不写成判断题，如实说明理由。代价：这两道题不再有可判的问题。\"; write the question with the period's last day as its due day (the follow-up survey may not exist that day; a further rule to build and prove).\n4610-  - Alex: \"确认：这类题不出题 (Recommended)\".\n4611-- **Decided:** a figure that covers a period which is not one fiscal or calendar year (a survey's rolling twelve months) and\n4612-  for which neither the topic nor the item gives a publication day is declined, with that reason. The cost he was shown: such\n4613-  topics get no judged question. This confirms the behaviour D414's refusal produced and that was reported as not confirmed.\n4614-- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step; mark N of the readers' form.\n4615-\n4616-## D418 · 2026-11-10 · A government's permission or ban on a class of product belongs to the theme, not to the company\n4617-\n4618-- **Asked:** \"“中国政府是否放行英伟达 H200 芯片在华销售”这类题，系统大多归在“英伟达”名下，有时归在行业主题“芯片出口管制”名下，同一道题三次归属还会不一致。第三次测试里归在公司名下的 5 份，两类读者都判为归错了，认为应归行业主题。区别是：归行业主题的题会给每家相关公司的判断都看到，归公司的只给这一家看。归哪边？\"\n4619-  - Options: the theme \"chip-export-controls\" (recommended): \"两类读者意见一致。我需要在提示词里加一条归属规则（政府对某类产品的放行或禁令归行业主题），并先小额验证不带坏别的题，比如法国对英伟达本身的反垄断调查仍归公司。\"; the company (the readers' form would then be changed to that reading).\n4620-  - Alex: \"归行业主题“芯片出口管制” (Recommended)\".\n4621-- **Decided:** a question about a government's or regulator's permission, restriction or ban on a class of products or trade\n4622-  belongs to the theme that covers it, also when the product is the company's own. A proceeding against the company itself (an\n4623-  investigation of its conduct, a fine) stays the company's. A rule in the request, proved small before any measurement, with\n4624-  the French investigation as the case that must not move.\n4625-- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step; mark O of the readers' form.\n4626-\n4627-## D419 · 2026-11-10 · The fourth Stage A is sent without asking again once each change is proved small and reviewed\n4628-\n4629-- **Asked:** \"上面你选的改动，各自小额验证通过并过评审之后，第四次正式测试（同样 44 道题各三次，约 0.11 美元；目前累计约 0.76 美元，上限 3 美元）怎么发？再测一次也不能保证一份错都没有，读者松紧不一的问题也还在。\"\n4630-  - Options: send once the checks pass (recommended): \"和上次一样：每项改动先单独小额验证并过评审，任何一项没通过就停下来找你，不发正式测试。\"; ask again before the send.\n4631-  - Alex: \"验证通过就直接发 (Recommended)\".\n4632:- **Decided:** as D415, for the changes of D416, D417 and D418: each is proved small and reviewed in the council; when all pass\n4633-  the fourth Stage A (the same 44 theses, three sends each, within D401's $3) is sent without asking again; a change that does\n4634-  not pass stops the line and goes to him. He was told that a further run cannot be promised to have no fault and that the\n4635-  reader families still part. Stage B still needs his word.\n4636-- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step.\n4637-\n4638-## D420 · 2026-11-10 · A proceeding that formally ends without the conclusion the question asks for is ruled out; the question stays\n4639-\n4640-- **Asked:** \"题目问的是“法国竞争管理局会不会在 2027 年 1 月 31 日前公布对英伟达反垄断调查的结论”。到期前可能有三种情况：① 公布结案决定（哪怕不处罚），算“发生了”；③ 调查还在继续，算“还在等”。这两点没有争议。有争议的是 ②：当局正式宣布放弃或撤回调查，但没有公布题目问的那种结论。模型每次写法不一样，读者也各执一词。② 算什么？\"\n4641-  - Options: it is ruled out (recommended): \"题目保持原样，问的仍是“有没有公布结论”。这类题固定有三种结果：公布了／当局正式放弃且没有结论／还在查。这也是目前多数已存答案的写法，且符合现有规则“判题目点名追踪的那件事”。不写“明确落空”的答案将算错。\"; ask instead whether the investigation is over (two outcomes; it tracks another event than the conclusion the thesis names).\n4642-  - Alex: \"② 算“明确落空” (Recommended)\".\n4643-- **Decided:** for a proceeding an authority conducts and whose asked-for event is its published decision or conclusion: a\n4644-  published closing decision, with or without a penalty, is the event happened; the authority formally abandoning or\n4645-  withdrawing the proceeding without that decision or conclusion is the event ruled out; the proceeding still going on the due\n4646-  day is the wait. Such an event always has a ruling out, and an answer that names none, or that writes the authority's\n4647-  decision to go on as the ruling out, is at fault. The judged question stays the one the thesis's outcome names.\n4648-- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step; mark R of the readers' form.\n4649-\n4650-## D421 · 2026-11-10 · Each further change is tested alone; all passing, the fourth Stage A is sent without asking again\n4651-\n4652-- **Asked:** \"接下来怎么走？我建议每项改动单独测，不再捆在一起：(a) 把你上一题的定义写进提示词，在三道法国调查题上单独测；(b) 把归属规则收窄成“题目追踪的是政府决定本身才归行业主题，追踪公司自己销售的仍归公司”，单独测；(c) 在 (a) 之后把“分两格填”再单独测一次，停止条件不变。调查题不出题那条直接并入。三项合计约 10 美分；第四次正式测试约 11 美分；目前累计 0.90 美元，上限 3 美元。\"\n4653-  - Options: test the three apart and send the fourth Stage A when all pass (recommended): \"(a)(b)(c) 各自小额验证并过评审。全部通过就直接发第四次正式测试；任何一项没通过就停下来找你。\"; drop the typed shape and do (a) and (b) only; test the three and ask before the fourth Stage A; stop here.\n4654-  - Alex: \"三项分别测，全过就直接发第四次 (Recommended)\".\n4655:- **Decided:** D417 goes into the working request. Then, each beside the working request and on its own: (a) D420's rule in the\n4656-  request, on the three French theses; (b) D418's sentence narrowed (the theme when the tracked outcome is the government's\n4657-  decision; the company when it is the company's own sales under it); (c) after (a), the typed ruling out once more, the same\n4658-  stop condition as before. Each is reviewed in the council. When all three pass, the fourth Stage A (the same 44 theses,\n4659-  three sends each, within D401's $3) is sent without asking again; one that does not pass stops the line and goes to him.\n4660-  Stage B still needs his word. This replaces D419's terms for these changes.\n4661-- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step.\n4662-\n4663-## D422 · 2026-11-10 · A second look by the model at its own answer is tested small, as a candidate; adoption is Alex's after the result\n4664-\n4665-- **Asked:** \"第四次正式测试仍有 3 条线各差 1 到 3 份。剩下的错都是同一种：模型懂规则，一遍写下来偶尔滑过去，事后问它它能自己指出来。我的建议是先做一个小额测试：让模型对自己的答案“再看一遍”（多发一次请求，只说“请对照规则逐条检查，没错就原样返回，有错就改正”，不提示哪里有错）。用第四次测试的 66 份已存答案（18 份读者公认有错、18 份有争议、30 份没人挑出错），约 7 美分。这和你定过的“复核要写在同一个提示词末尾”不一样，所以必须由你定。下一步怎么走？\"\n4666-  - Options: the small test of a second look (recommended): \"只是候选做法，不是已证明的修法。通过条件事先写死：18 份公认有错的至少改好 9 份，且 30 份没错的最多改坏 1 份；第二遍的答案若过不了程序检查就沿用第一遍。改过的答案由两类读者盲读。通过也只说明“值得带着它再正式测一次”，不等于六条线过了。若采用，每道新题多一次请求，约多花 0.1 美分和 10 到 20 秒。做完我把结果报给你，再由你定是否采用。\"; go on class by class (the unjustified declines first); open Stage B on the step as it stands (his to waive his lines); stop.\n4667-  - Alex: \"先做“再看一遍”的小额测试 (Recommended)\".\n4668-- **Decided:** the test designed in `clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/probe-second-look-2026-11-10/DESIGN.md` is run: 66 stored\n4669-  answers of the fourth Stage A (18 with a fault the readers agree on, 18 with a disputed one only, 30 that no reader\n4670-  faults), each sent back once with one instruction that names no fault; the changed answers read blind by the two reader\n4671-  families; passing means at least 9 of the 18 mended and at most 1 of the 30 damaged. A second answer that code refuses\n4672-  leaves the first in place. The result goes to him, and whether the step takes a second look is decided by him then: this\n4673-  decision opens the test and nothing more. It is a departure, for this test, from AGENTS §6's check at the end of the same\n4674-  prompt, which stays in the request.\n4675-- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step.\n4676-\n4677-## D423 · 2026-11-10 · Work on Jev's revision relation stops; \"a later version does not take the older record's questions\" is accepted as a direction and, once measured, withdrawn by its author; the rule stays, pending Alex\n4678-\n4679-- **Asked** (after the traced case of the Step 2 log §15): \"建议停止在 Jev 的“更新关系”上投入。它作为已知缺陷留在清单上 … Step 2 和 Jev 都不改。\" and\n4680-  \"有一件事等你定，不急。… B 被判为 A 的更新版后，要不要让 B 自动挂到 A 的所有问题下面？ 不自动挂（我的建议）：这次带进去的 5 条里，2 条错、1 条说不清、\n4681-  2 条有用。 保持自动挂。\"\n4682-  - Alex: \"okay take your suggestion what is the fix and how to measure get your council skill ready to propose\".\n4683-- **Decided by those words:** no further work on Jev's revision relation now; the defect stays open with its counts. The direction\n4684-  \"not automatically\" is accepted, and the council loop is to propose the fix and its measurement before anything is built.\n4685-- **What the council round found** (`clean-arch/step2-revision-links-2026-11-10/LOG.md`): on the three saved draws the rule wrote 24\n4686-  links (5 of 700, 11 of 725, 8 of 730). Two blind reader families: 19 context by both, 3 evidence by both, 2 split. Nothing a\n4687-  program can read separates the two kinds. One context link judged both ways: rung 2 in six of six. One evidence link judged both\n4688-  ways (NVIDIA's answer beside four reports under FY2028 revenue): rung 2, 2, 2 with it and 2, 3, 2 without, not decided by the rule\n4689-  fixed beforehand. The suggestion rested on draw 1 alone and is withdrawn by its author; Codex agrees that the rule is not changed\n4690-  now and does not agree that the present rule is shown to be better.\n--\n4845-- **Scope:** clean Step 1; c8 stays in force.\n4846-\n4847:## D436 · 2026-11-13 · One bet seen from two sides is one question; change 3 is dropped; G1-a and G1-b run without it\n4848-\n4849-- **Asked**, after two blind source readers agreed on none of six cases (`clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/gate1/PREREAD-RESULT.md`):\n4850-  \"例子：同一篇文章里有'2027 年 HBM 出货增长多少'和'2027 年 HBM 是否仍然供不应求'。两位读者对照原文判：一位说这是两个能分别押注的题，另一位说是同一件事的两面，放一张卡就够。…你怎么看：这类情况应该算一个题还是两个题？\"\n4851-  - Options: one question, change 3 dropped (recommended): \"第二件事作为同一题的背景留着（后面判断时显示为'不判'），第三处改动作废。理由：都是同一个押注的不同侧面；我们的原则是偏谨慎、不要把一件事拆成碎题。\"; two questions, change 3 continues; case by case.\n4852-  - Alex: \"算一个题，第三处不改 (Recommended)\".\n4853-- **Asked:** \"第三处停下后，这两处的小测试（42 次发送，约 0.6 美元，上限 2 美元）要不要照常跑？\" Options: run (recommended): \"这两处不依赖第三处。任何一项不过就停，报给你。\"; wait. Alex: \"照常跑 (Recommended)\".\n4854-- **Decided:** a second side of the same bet (the shortage beside the shipments, the AI-chip share beside the chip total, the capacity keeping pace beside the demand) is one question; it stays as context in that question and is shown as not judged (D397). Change 3 (the `outcome` definition) is dropped, and the \"two bets in one thesis\" class is closed as not a Step 1 defect under this ruling. G1-a and G1-b run as fixed in `COMBINED-PLAN.md`; the candidate for later gates is c8 with changes 1 and 2 only.\n4855-- **Scope:** clean Step 1; c8 stays in force.\n4856-\n4857-## D437 · 2026-11-13 · Carry changes 1 and 2 to gate 2 although the year line was missed\n4858-\n4859-- **Asked**, with `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/gate1/G1A-READING.md` and `G1B-READING.md`: \"第一关的结果：'客户那句'的改动过了；'今年明年各开一题'没过。…新版 9 次里只有 5 次把两年分开开题，事先定的线是 9 次至少 8 次。旧版 c8 是 0 次。…新写法 26 次里 20 次分开，旧版 26 次里 0 次。没分开的那几次，模型都读到了规则，但觉得'两年都开太多了'，只留一年。下一步怎么走？\"\n4860-  - Options: carry both changes to gate 2 (recommended by Claude): \"分年虽然没达线，但从 0 次升到大约四分之三，而且'两年塞一题'完全消失，没发现带坏别的东西。第二关在存档上查它会不会弄坏周边情况（重复文章、同一量的另一种口径、延期的事等，约 1.5 美元，线先给你看）。代价：等于在看到结果后放宽了我自己定的线。\"; stop the year change and carry only the customer sentence (the reviewer, `council/lx-codex.md`, recommended stopping the year change and keeping c8); stop both and keep c8.\n4861-  - Alex: \"带着两处改动进第二关 (Recommended)\".\n4862-- **Decided:** the candidate for gate 2 is c15yc (c8 with the year boundary and the scoped capacity counterexample). The year line's failure stays recorded as a failure (5 of 9 against 8 of 9); it is not presented as a pass. Gate 2's lines are written, reviewed and shown to Alex before any send. c8 stays in force.\n4863-- **Scope:** clean Step 1.\n4864-\n4865-## D438 · 2026-11-13 · Send gate 2\n4866-\n4867-- **Asked**, with `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/GATE2.md` (version 11, reviewed clean in `council/mi-codex.md`): \"第二关审完了，要发吗？…新版做错的次数比旧版多 3 次以上（9 次里），就停下报给你。共 126 次发送，约 1.8 美元，上限 2.2 美元。\" Options: send (recommended): \"先跑完 126 次。我和一位盲读者各自逐条读，有分歧的一律算新版错。任何一条停止线被触发就停下报给你；全过的话再设计第三关（在新文章上新旧版对比），也先给你看。\"; do not send.\n4868-- Alex: \"发 (Recommended)\".\n4869-- **Decided:** gate 2 is sent as written; a fired stop or an unexercised control goes to Alex; a pass leads to gate 3's design, shown to him before any send. c8 stays in force.\n4870-\n4871-## D439 · 2026-11-13 · While Alex is not active, the council decides by consensus and the loop iterates to the PRD's production goals\n4872-\n4873-- **Alex, 2026-11-13** (unprompted, after a recap of the goal): \"把这个goal 改成更多的要求council in the loop 来自行的根据数据和目标做决策。我接下来不会active,需要你有问题的时候就fire council 然后和claude 掰扯直到你们能达到共识为止再下去执行，并仔细的测量，自己看trace 然后把每一轮log 做学习总结，不要饭一样的错，词学迭代完成我们的PRD生产目标\".\n4874-- **Decided (his words):** while he is not active, every choice or next step that would have gone to him goes to the council: an independent read-only Codex review and Claude argue it on the data, the PRD and its quantified goals until they reach a consensus; the consensus is recorded as a decision citing D439, executed, measured, every trace read by Claude itself, and every round logged with a learning summary so the same mistake is not made twice; the loop iterates until the PRD's production goals are met.\n4875-- **Settled by Claude (wording and limits, not confirmed by Alex):** the standing limits of AGENTS.md stay (the frozen ruler never changes; nothing pushed, deployed, published or committed unasked; credentials and provider caps untouched). Opening a new version of a piece frozen for \"a new version only Alex opens\" is a council decision under D439; the frozen ruler is not. A disagreement the council cannot settle is recorded with both positions and the cheaper, reversible course is taken. **Spending ceiling:** paid model calls in this period stay within $40 at published rates in total, each paid step with its own ceiling in its council-agreed design; this figure is Claude's setting, not Alex's, and is reported in every status update.\n4876-- **Where written:** AGENTS.md, \"Authority and scope\" (the D439 bullet) and §7.3 \"Own the loop\"; `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md`; the memory file `feedback-council-decides-while-alex-away.md`. The session goal itself is set by Alex's `/goal` command; the replacement text is given to him in the reply.\n4877-- **Scope:** all modules Alex has taken up; the current work is clean Step 1 (gates 2 and 3 of `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/COMBINED-PLAN.md`), then the Step 4 judgement faults that kept Stage B from passing.\n4878-\n4879-## D440 · 2026-11-13 · Gate 2 failed; a memory diagnostic decides whether c15yc goes on (council consensus under D439)\n4880-\n4881-- **Council** (D439; Alex not active): an independent Codex member and Claude argued four rounds (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mj-*`). Agreed facts: gate 2 failed under its declared rules (two stop lines on the memory article); the link line measured the wrong thing (c8's request returns an uncovered statement with empty links); the 3-of-9 against 0-of-9 memory-thesis difference is real and its cause is not established. The council's first position was to keep c8; Claude's was a larger re-send. The consensus, after Claude adopted the council's changes (a margin fixed in advance, a three-way result in which inconclusive is not a pass, retained statements decisive, an exercised-control rule, a named and simulation-validated interval): \"Council position: consensus on the rule in mj-challenge-2.md as amended by mj-challenge-3.md\" (`mj-codex-4.md`).\n4882-- **Decided:** the diagnostic in `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/gate2/MEMORY-DIAGNOSTIC.md` runs (108 sends, ceiling $2.0); its rule is `gate2/memory_rule.py`, frozen by sha256. c15yc goes on to gate 3's design only on \"proceed\" for both decisive outcomes; otherwise c8 stays and the council decides the next step. The gate-2 failure stays recorded.\n--\n5173-- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mt-codex-9.md`): \"Write and independently review the status report first; then\n5174-  continue to the $0 identity-design comparison, with F6 recorded as a contradiction whose standalone impact remains uncertain.\"\n5175:- **Decided:** F6 is not tested on its own; its correction, with the date safeguards of round 8 (no invented release day; D417 intact), waits\n5176-  for the next clean Step 1 version and is not bundled silently. Next, a status report for Alex (goal, results under both treatments,\n5177-  what traces can and cannot establish, Stage A failed, Stage B's full-run reading largely unmeasured, D427 outstanding, production's\n5178-  unlinked facts not a shown loss, opening opportunities not right answers), reviewed by the council for accuracy; then the $0 comparison of\n5179-  a general prompt change against a matching-stage design for the identity boundaries.\n5180-\n5181-## D463 · 2026-11-13 · The identity lever: a general prompt clause first (P), written and probe-designed before any send (council consensus under D439)\n5182-\n5183-- **Comparison** (`clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/step1-audit/IDENTITY-COMPARISON.md`): production, which also sees the open\n5184-  questions, says \"a different population, source, estimate, wording or direction of a question is the same question; a different\n5185-  quantity, period or decision is another\" and opens both capex years in 5 of 6 draws and the Ohio signing in 4 of 6 (clean c8: 1 and 1);\n5186-  production never opens a memory question (0 of 6), and the stopped c14/c15yc year sentence moved c8's memory question (D441). A matching\n5187-  stage cannot recover a question Step 1 never proposes unless Step 1 stops judging identity (a larger architectural change).\n5188-- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mt-codex-12.md`): production is a lead, not a controlled proof (its workflow\n5189-  proposes candidates that may already be open and code compares them afterward); P can repeat the memory regression; \"a different\n5190-  quantity, period or decision is another\" is too broad alone (a later deadline of one event is evidence while the earlier is open; a\n5191-  comparison names two periods and asks one); the unsigned-deal case permits a separate question when independently worthwhile; two or\n5192-  three general examples per class; a frozen fresh-article probe with reader-marked expectations, denominators, minimum effects, an\n5193-  inconclusive outcome and exercised positive controls. \"Proceed to a general written P candidate and a reviewed fresh-article probe design\n5194-  with these corrections; do not send until the cases, controls, thresholds and regression handling are concrete and the council has\n5195-  reviewed them.\"\n5196-- **Decided:** write the candidate (c16, from c8, the identity clause only; F6 not included) and the probe design (fresh articles after\n5197-  2026-07-14 never sent in a Step 1 measurement, frozen before any answer is read, an independent reader's expected behaviour per article,\n5198-  a full-run draw's library at 2026-07-14 as a controlled snapshot, the stopped capex, Ohio and memory articles as guards), both reviewed by\n5199-  the council before any send.\n5200-\n5201-## D464 · 2026-11-13 · Send the case-specific identity diagnostic, c16 version 5 against c8, under one $5 ledger (council consensus under D439)\n5202-\n5203-- **Rounds** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mt-codex-13.md`–`mt-codex-15.md`): the candidate went through four blind audits\n5204-  (versions 1, 3, 4 read by fresh Codex readers; version 5 answers the last, wording-level points); the selection was redone with four\n5205-  blind category readers over 80 candidates and twenty more for T1 and T3, which showed that this window holds **one fresh story per target\n5206-  boundary** (next year's hyperscaler capex; the OpenAI Ohio guarantee) and no independent positive comparison story; the design became a\n5207-  case-specific diagnostic: targets reported per story, regression lines on 7 merge stories, 9 negative stories and the stored guards\n5208-  (memory with nine sends a state and a stop on D441's shape, capex-repeat-a, population), validity minima, article-to-story counting, one\n5209-  invocation and one ledger. Round 15's two blocks were fixed and proved at $0: a memory validity minimum (7 valid sends a state) and the\n5210-  ledger settling missing, malformed or zero-priced usage at its reservation (`identity-probe/probe_identity.py`, five tests, a mutant\n--\n5291-  permanent product start; D370 allows a real existing library); the three open shapes are not tuning targets and stay recorded concerns\n5292-  (D373), each still judged case by case by the standard. The candidate L2 (\"an outcome that leads with one figure names its main one\") is\n5293:  not sent: order alone is wider than the step's rule and D436. Next, at $0: every \"no main figure or event\" refusal of the Stage A runs, with\n5294-  its thesis and the readers' marks, judged by a blind reader for what the outcome itself names as tracked; candidate wordings checked against\n5295-  counterexamples (ordered but with no main one) before any probe.\n5296-\n5297-## D470 · 2026-11-13 · The ladder-refusal candidate stops; the 41 Stage A splits are recorded, eight with a provisional reading from D414; Stage A's verdict is unchanged (council consensus under D439)\n5298-\n5299-- **Boundary check** (`clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/ladder-refusal/`): a truly blind reader (`blind-verdicts.md`, key `blind-key.json`) agrees with\n5300-  the first reader on 9 of 12 \"main figure\" verdicts; the four cases both call \"one main\" were refused in 9 of 48 stored sends; the candidate\n5301-  clause would change one case by the reader's application and risks joining separately tracked things in seven; the candidate is not sent.\n5302-- **Splits** (`stage-a-splits/splits.json`, 41): eight due-day splits read provisionally by D414 (a month such as \"~February 2027\" is no stated day,\n5303-  so code's day holds); the others stay recorded disputes (the ninth due-day split is a basis label; the stake and Firmus \"main figure\" points,\n5304-  the Vera CPU event, the H100 theme coverage, the reference rule, the named faults). Stage A's verdict does not move under any reading: lines\n5305-  1–4 fail on agreed faults (7 marks on 6 answers), and 22 of 40 theses are right by a written ladder against the diagnostic 26.\n5306-- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mu-codex-8.md`, `mu-codex-9.md`): \"停止当前拒绝规则候选，不发送；保留原始分歧和明确的暂定解释，不宣称 16 处全部解决。\n5307-  将正确拒绝如何影响上线要求作为待决定的问题，由 council 先按 D439 讨论；Alex 的后续回答随时优先。\"\n5308-- **Decided:** as quoted. Open for the council under D439: whether a correct refusal of a thesis the ladder step cannot judge should count\n5309-  against the gate's written-ladder line (D400), which measures Step 1's shapes and the ladder step together.\n5310-\n5311-## D471 · 2026-11-13 · The written-ladder line stands; the ten \"right only by refusal\" theses traced; one period-rule candidate (c17) probed on stored cases (council consensus under D439)\n5312-\n5313-- **Line question** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mu-codex-10.md`): \"保持 D400 的通过线\": a correct refusal counts as right, not as a\n5314-  written ladder; Alex's line stays as he wrote it.\n5315-- **Census** (`clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/refused-shapes/`): the ten theses right but not by a written ladder, by the accounting rule\n5316-  (reproducing 32 / 22 / 40); the model's own accounts (neutral question, the tested ledger, $0.0295): three come from the period rule read as a\n5317-  horizon (\"a calendar-2027 full-year average — beyond next year, barred\" from a July 2026 item; a survey's rolling twelve months twice); four\n5318-  from the contested \"main figure\" boundary (the second part seen as a consequence or another measure); one kept two figures knowingly; two are\n5319-  the H100 theme-coverage dispute (`ACCOUNTS-RESULT.md`).\n5320-- **Council** (`mu-codex-11.md` to `mu-codex-13.md`): the period candidate is sourced (§3 D \"自然年的今年或明年\") but must protect a comparison with the\n5321-  year before, count no non-opening as a fix, set valid-send minima and a comparison-shape exercise minimum, and be audited blind in its final\n5322-  version. **Decided:** candidate c17 (c8 with the shared-quantity period sentence clarified, +236 characters; version 2 after a blind audit; the\n5323-  version-2 audit found no contradiction, wording-level risks only) probed on stored states under `period-probe/PERIOD-PROBE-DESIGN.md`: three\n5324-  target openings, the memory states (nine sends a state, D441's comparison shape guarded), the capex states, the federal opening; 96 jobs,\n5325-  about $1.4, a $2 ceiling. A pass leads only to a council decision on fresh articles.\n5326-\n5327-## D472 · 2026-11-13 · A budget exception for the period probe: the nine never-sent jobs are sent before any answer is read (council consensus under D439)\n5328-\n--\n5378-  the article that opened it and the library at that step, without the system's thesis or reason; they write the questions worth tracking\n5379-  that the source supports, judging \"worth asking\" apart from \"can be laddered\" (one main figure for one period, or one event with a date;\n5380:  D417's rolling windows not); only then are they shown the thesis and say whether one of theirs is the same matter and what it loses.\n5381-  Counted by distinct matter and by run; disagreements kept. No automatic threshold: the council weighs distinct matters, expected effect,\n5382-  regression risk and cost before any structural diagnostic, which is designed and reviewed before any send.\n5383-\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '问题怎么写|同一题、续期|开题理由|<h[123]' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '问题怎么写|同一题、续期|开题理由|<h[123]' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"145:  <h1>抽取与开题标准</h1>\n162:<h3>一张图：同一篇文章里每句话的去向</h3>\n184:<h2 id=\"decisions\"><span class=\"num\">已拍</span>Alex 拍板的 12 条</h2>\n194:<tr><td>2</td><td>\"共同量\"按 D191 落实：任何一家公司之外、好几家都会受它影响的量或价格（合计支出、合约价、利率）都可以开题，开题理由叫 <code>shared_quantity</code>；期间按自然年。提示词和代码要跟着改</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 3 节 D 类</td></tr>\n207:<h3 id=\"d248\">D248：颗粒度的七条（2026-10-30）</h3>\n222:<h3 id=\"d250\">D250：证据的四条界线和计数单位（2026-10-31）</h3>\n235:<h3 id=\"conventions\">我定的记录约定</h3>\n244:<h2 id=\"words\"><span class=\"num\">1</span>这一页用的词：一词一义</h2>\n253:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">开题理由</td><td>候选问题值得开的几类理由之一，答案里写在 <code>opens_as</code><span class=\"src\">D184；英文 admission reason</span></td><td></td></tr>\n263:<h2 id=\"ledger\"><span class=\"num\">2</span>账本里记三种东西</h2>\n266:<li><b>问题</b>问题句、结果档、到期日写下不改；当前判断随证据更新，到期定格<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。问题分标的和主题，按开题理由分五类（第 3 节）。问题从三处来：文章里的候选问题；用户的备忘录<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 State</span>：\"A thesis from the user's memo is not yet judged until evidence first links to it\"；分析员开始覆盖一家公司时种下的驱动问题<span class=\"src\">D208，设计未建</span>。</li>\n271:<h2 id=\"types\"><span class=\"num\">3</span>问题的五类：账本的几大类型</h2>\n272:<p>开题理由是 D184 定的四类，D236 把主驱动量扩到产品节点，所以写成五类。判两件事，互不顶替：这是谁的问题（标的还是主题）；为什么值得开（开题理由）。</p>\n274:<thead><tr><th>类</th><th>开题理由</th><th>标的或主题</th><th>问什么</th><th>量还是事件</th><th>期间和到期</th><th>核对材料 <code>settled_by</code></th><th>出处</th></tr></thead>\n292:<h3>五类之外的东西去哪</h3>\n297:<li><b>开题理由是封闭的</b><span class=\"src\">D184</span>：一件事属不属于五类之一，按上表逐条看，比如一个监管决定看它是不是 E 类。哪一类都不属于的不开；它是不是证据、挂到哪，照第 5 节和归档规则。</li>\n300:<h3>问题怎么写：PRD 06 的梯子规则，不重写</h3>\n308:<h2 id=\"opening\"><span class=\"num\">4</span>开题标准</h2>\n310:<p>颗粒度按一个高端对冲基金分析员：只有会单独下注的大事开题，鸡毛蒜皮不开题（它的陈述留不留照第 5 节判）；同一个赌注的几种说法是一题，截止日、里程碑、财年和日历年各按本节\"同一题、续期，还是另一题\"里的那一条判<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</p>\n313:<h3>四个测试<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6</span></h3>\n327:<h3>不开的<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6 的清单</span></h3>\n337:<tr><td>以约束性义务为理由开：公司自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。它们不是约束性义务；对别的问题仍可以是证据，或按别的开题理由判</td><td>D236、D238</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n343:<h3>同一题、续期，还是另一题：匹配这一步的事，抽取不判库里的</h3>\n355:<li><b>共同量：</b>以共同量理由开题、带量的候选（量的类别是 <code>other</code> 的不算），由代码按\"主题＋量＋期间\"判同一题；政策阶段和别的事件保留按事件判的身份；不带这个开题理由的主题量由模型判<span class=\"src\">D197</span>。</li>\n358:<h3>谁判，谁查</h3>\n362:<tr><td>测试 1–3、同一篇文章里的测试 4、属于哪一类、问题怎么写</td><td>抽取的模型（判断）</td></tr>\n364:<tr><td>和库里的同一题、续期、另一题</td><td>匹配（Jev）和碰撞裁决<span class=\"src\">D190</span>；共同量由代码<span class=\"src\">D197</span></td></tr>\n368:<h2 id=\"evidence\"><span class=\"num\">5</span>证据标准</h2>\n369:<h3>5.1 留的规则和四类</h3>\n386:<h3>5.2 不完整也是证据</h3>\n389:<h3>5.3 不留的<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2 的清单，加 D238、D243 的行</span></h3>\n408:<h3>5.4 一条记录必须保住的意思<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §3，原样</span></h3>\n423:<h3>5.5 来源层<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 的四层；D238 采纳的 role-v29 原文</span></h3>\n438:<h2 id=\"weight\"><span class=\"num\">6</span>分量</h2>\n449:<h3>判法</h3>\n460:<h2 id=\"views\"><span class=\"num\">7</span>研究观点标准</h2>\n471:<h2 id=\"golden\"><span class=\"num\">8</span>金标：改提示词的测试标准</h2>\n483:<h3>每一条记什么</h3>\n487:<li><b>问题：</b>必须开的（类、开题理由、标的或主题、要点、<code>settled_by</code>）；可以开的（另一种合理写法）；不该开的（第 4 节哪一行或哪个测试）。</li>\n491:<h3>分量的分布（定稿）</h3>\n500:<h3>怎么写成、怎么核的</h3>\n518:<h3>用它之前要知道的</h3>\n526:<h2 id=\"method\"><span class=\"num\">9</span>改提示词、测量、迭代</h2>\n529:<h3>9.1 改提示词</h3>\n539:<h3>9.2 测量</h3>\n566:<h3>9.3 迭代：一类一类改</h3>\n578:<h2 id=\"rulings\"><span class=\"num\">10</span>Alex 已经拍过的判例</h2>\n611:<h2 id=\"conflicts\"><span class=\"num\">11</span>在用的标准之间的冲突，怎么摆平</h2>\n639:<h2 id=\"checks\"><span class=\"num\">12</span>校验记录和出处</h2>\n640:<h3>三轮独立读者仿真</h3>\n654:<h3>十一轮漂移检查</h3>\n676:<h3>出处</h3>\n679:<h3>文件</h3>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/reachability/packet-phase1.json\\\")); [(print(\\\"\\\\nCASE\\\",x[\\\"case\\\"],\\\"DATE\\\",x[\\\"article\\\"][\\\"publication_day\\\"],\\\"TITLE\\\",x[\\\"article\\\"][\\\"title\\\"],\\\"\\\\n\\\",x[\\\"article\\\"][\\\"text\\\"],\\\"\\\\nOPEN:\\\",\\\" | \\\".join(q[\\\"description\\\"] for q in x[\\\"library_before\\\"])) for x in p if 7<=x[\\\"case\\\"]<=10]'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
